+# Solution
+
+`sheet/engine.py` uses a small recursive-descent parser for formulas and a memoized depth-first evaluator for cell references.
+
+The parser implements the specified precedence and associativity rules, including right-associative exponentiation and unary minus binding below exponentiation. It also supports parentheses, insignificant whitespace, decimal numbers, and forward or transitive cell references.
+
+Cell values are cached after evaluation. Cells currently being evaluated are tracked so direct and indirect dependency cycles raise `CycleError`. Normal Python arithmetic behavior is preserved, including `ZeroDivisionError` for division by zero.
